# [Create a shape]($heading.id('shape'))

`zml.Shape` holds metadata including the element type, dimension sizes, and tags.
[Shape source](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/zml/shape.zig)

- `zml.Shape.init(dimensions, dtype)`\
  `Shape`. Use a tuple such as `.{ 2, 3 }` for sizes or named fields such as `.{ .output = 2, .feature = 3 }` to assign tags as well.
- `zml.Shape.scalar(dtype)`\
  `Shape`. Describe one element with zero axes.

# [Read the element type and axes]($heading.id('element-type-and-axes'))

- `shape.rank()` / `shape.dtype()`\
  `u4` number of axes / `DataType` element type.
- `shape.dim(axis)` / `shape.axis(axis)`\
  `i64` size / `u3` index. Accept a numeric axis or a tag.

See [Dimension tags]($link.page('zml/concepts').ref('dimension-tags')) for an
example of selecting axes by name.

# [Read sizes and element count]($heading.id('sizes-and-element-count'))

- `shape.dims()`\
  `[]const i64`. Borrow the ordered sizes from the shape. Keep the shape alive while using the slice.
- `shape.count()`\
  `usize`. Return the number of elements.
